  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1229 AM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nDespite a rather progressive storm track and southern stream \npattern, the forecast looks mainly dry beyond Monday morning. \nTemperatures will be much cooler Monday through Friday of the \nHoliday week, as highs only climb into the 50s and 60s each day. A \nseries of disturbances will swing through north Texas next week, but \nrain chances look minimal with little surface moisture to work with \nand a lack of quality sfc to 700 mb moisture. By Thanksgiving day, \nwe may have our coldest morning of the season so far, with lows \nlikely dipping into the lower to middle 30s over the Hill Country \nand the upper 30s to upper 40s elsewhere. The Thanksgiving holiday \nitself will be cool, with partly to mostly sunny skies and highs in \nthe 50s and 60s.",
